course: dictionary
lesson: 6597
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Noel is a good example. It can mean Christmas, a Christmas song called a carol, or a name.
explain: Look for clues. «The First Noel» is a famous Christmas song, so noel there means a carol. In «Who were the first to cry Nowell?» the spelling is old-fashioned, but Nowell is another spelling of Noel, and the word cry tells you it is a shout of joy.
explain: To check your meaning, put it into the sentence. If the words around it are about singing, church or Christmas, the carol or Christmas meaning fits. If it is a person's name, it starts with a capital letter and is about someone, not a season.
fact: Noel can mean Christmas, a Christmas carol, or a name.
fact: Noel is a noun. As a name, Noel is for boys and Noelle is for girls.
fact: «The First Noel» is a famous carol that people sing at Christmas.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, the field mice sing a carol at Mole's door.
fact: In French, «Noël» means Christmas.
exercise: The choir sang a beautiful noel at the church. What does noel mean here? | A kind of boat | A type of bird | *A Christmas carol | A summer holiday
exercise: Noel was late for the school play, so the teacher waited. What kind of word is Noel in this sentence? | *A name | A kind of snow | A Christmas card | A shout of joy
exercise: «Who were the first to cry Nowell?» Nowell is an old spelling of which word? | Befell | Carol | *Noel | Animals
test: In French, «Noël» means which English word? | Holiday | *Christmas | Summer | Birthday
test: Which of these uses noel as a name? | Carols were sung at noel | We sang a noel in the church hall | *Noel and his sister went to the park after school | The shop had a big noel display in the window
exam: «Animals all, as it befell.» What does befell mean? | Was lost | *Happened | Sang loudly | Ran away
